{
 "_about": "Parts, gear and colours of the operator models made by make_operators.py. Coordinates: Blender rest pose, metres, Z up, the character faces -Y, its left is +X. Colours are sRGB hex (as the game shows them). Part 'colors' map the pack's material names to the model's materials ('*' = any other), 'rules' (in order, a later one wins) pick faces by source material 'mat', dominant bones 'bones', face centre 'box' / 'out', 'normal' and give them another material ('to') or 'delete' them; 'decimate' (ratio) thins a part. Gear types: shell (cloth over the outfit surface: faces 'on' materials inside 'box', not in 'out', cut by 'cut' / 'planes'; 'hide' deletes the outfit faces under it, 'subdiv' makes smaller faces for a 'pattern'), pouch (box on the surface, also patches, plates, rails), strap, tube ('snap' lays it on the surface built so far), box, cyl, helmet (ellipsoid shell above a 'rim', grown to 'fit' the head); 'bone' puts an item 100 % on one bone; 'mirror' adds the same item on the other side; 'zone' says which envelope it is checked against.",
 "envelope": {
  "_about": "Gear envelope agreed with CharacterBody's hitboxes: torso gear (carriers, rigs, pouches, straps) inside y front..back and |x| <= half_x for z in z (straps on the shoulders |x| <= strap_x); belt gear inside the belt box; head gear inside the ellipsoid, small items (goggles, NVG mount, mask filters, smaller than small_size) may reach y small_front; limb gear at most max_off off the outfit surface; a tight layer over the head (the knit of a balaclava, it also covers the jaw, which lies outside the head ellipsoid itself) at most layer.max_off off it; nothing below the soles.",
